{
  "_": "The ONE menu of this element's Telegram Mini App and of its «Working process» in the core (node steps 789, 790). Telegram draws it in the drawer of /tg; the core's left menu draws the same tree through the door GET /api/tg-menu. Edit only here: an item added here appears in both windows. Every `slug` is a screen folder in ../_pages/<slug>/ (the empty slug is the branch's own page). A category opens downward: its `children` are the element's own things (projects, authors, services), written by its agent; `add` names the new-item line. Modes: «work» — the person's own projects; «a2a» — the element's services sold outward through Lagrix (a precedent while the network is not live). `common` — the items OUTSIDE the modes, on the same level as «My projects» and «A2A · Web4» (the owner, Telegram 757): subscriptions, cron automation, the element's settings, help; shown in every mode. An element may drop a mode or an item; subscriptions and cron stay in every element.",
